// A unique is set inside a `for`: to what the last entity that sets it
// gives, in the order of the `for`, when the `for` ends (`ent.accumulate`
// with the rule `set`). An integer, a float, a bool, an enum, an entity;
// as it was where no entity sets it; and read in the same `for`, as it
// was before. However the `for` ran.
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/set_unique.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.out
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/set_unique.ent 2>/dev/null | cmp - %t.out
// RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t.out
// RUN: ent-translate --import-ent %S/Inputs/set_unique.ent -I %S/../../devices \
// RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=IR

// IR: ent.accumulate @Seen "n" set

// CHECK:      17 8.5 true true false last 36 rounds 11 was 1
// CHECK-NEXT: it is 17
// CHECK-NEXT: 17 8.5 true true false last 36 rounds 22 was 12
// CHECK-NEXT: it is 17
